{
  "id": "ss.char.hourglass",
  "name": "Hourglass",
  "description": "The wasp of the eight, and it knows it. Venom-green hair in two buns, lids half down over both eyes, a smirk pulled to one side. The dress is the hourglass it used to be — broad at the shoulder, pinched to nothing at the waist, flaring to a striped skirt with the wasp's dark bands on it — and two pale wings lie folded off the shoulders behind. From the near hand, held out, swings the chained head: a Soldier's head-plate packed solid on a cord, hanging and swinging even when the body is still, because a thing that heavy never quite stops. Same dead organ as the rest, worn as a brooch; same bobble feelers. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
